Buddhism: a defended scholarly study (@buddhist-research-completion: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @buddhism) { r_7QF5XWQYY7K78XPCQMM068YYE9
Complete the [core reading](Core-completion.lingua#r_562HHAD8ARXMYG8DC0GP1QKYAT) and a [sustained investigation](Research-study.lingua#r_5KS9ZFFK5HYPAMBYJQ9ACHF3NJ) at an explicitly stated scope. The advanced outcome is a defended study, not a claim to exhaustive knowledge of Buddhism or to a religious attainment.

The finished account identifies its question, corpus, editions, relevant language evidence, and the interpretation it defends. It represents a serious competing explanation fairly, places its argument within the scholarship actually consulted, and answers informed criticism through a documented revision. State what remains unresolved and which evidence could change the conclusion.

Prior notes and investigations can supply useful evidence without being repeated merely to fit a sequence. Readings and links remain available at every depth. Broaden or deepen the research when its question calls for it, using the same ordinary Records and sources.

An optional comparison with [Yoga](../../yoga/Yoga.lingua#r_017AAD0FQ294F8HBVVTQAZ55GH) can examine similar language about discipline or liberation after the Buddhist core. [Iyengar’s Light on Yoga](../../yoga/sources/Light-on-Yoga.lingua#r_7F91WKD2ZF75XE12E244GF0FXF) belongs to that separate reading path; its account should first be understood on its own terms.

**Return:** [Buddhism: from the path to sustained inquiry](../Buddhism.lingua#r_7P61Z6HHZNZZ8ND3DHXSFSNRRE).
